===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|en|cœlacanth||obsolete}}

===Etymology===
From the {{bor|en|NL.|-}} genus name {{taxlink|Coelacanthus|genus}}, from {{der|en|grc|κοῖλος||hollow}} + {{m|grc|ἄκανθα||spine}}, referring to the hollow [[caudal fin]] rays of the first fossil specimen described and named by {{w|Louis Agassiz}} in 1839.<ref>{{R:Etymonline}}</ref>

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈsiː.lə.kænθ/}}
* {{audio|en|En-us-coelacanth.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{audio|en|En-coelacanth.ogg|Audio}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# Either of two species of deep-water fish, {{taxlink|Latimeria chalumnae|species|noshow=1}} of the [[Indian Ocean]] and {{taxlink|Latimeria menadoensis|species|noshow=1}} of [[Indonesia]].
# Any [[lobe]]-[[finned]] fish in the order [[Coelacanthiformes]], thought until 1938 to have been [[extinct]] for 70 million years.

